* Fix flaky ness of opennav_docking test_docking_server (<a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="2817948689" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/ros-navigation/navigation2/issues/4878" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/ros-navigation/navigation2/issues/4878/hovercard" href="https://github.com/ros-navigation/navigation2/issues/4878">#4878</a>) (<a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="2817980741" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/ros-navigation/navigation2/issues/4879" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/ros-navigation/navigation2/pull/4879/hovercard" href="https://github.com/ros-navigation/navigation2/pull/4879">#4879</a>)

Call publish() (odom -&gt; base_link tf) at startup to kick things off and
spin 10 times(1 second) TF, so that it has a chance to propogate to the
docking_server so that it will accept an action request.

Previously it was only spinning once, hoping the timer would fire and
call publish fast enough for it to propogate to the docking_server
so that it is able to accept the first 'dock_robot' action request

Signed-off-by: Mike Wake &lt;macwake@gmail.com&gt;

